## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the UQ Lakes Bus Board project.

### Implementation Summary

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I've installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite application.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependencies

**2. Code Integration**
- **File Modified:** `src/App.js`
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
  - Added the `<Analytics />` component inside the main `<App>` component's return statement
  - The Analytics component is placed just before the closing `</main>` tag, after the `<ToastContainer />` component

### Framework-Specific Implementation

The implementation follows the React/Vite-specific instructions from the official documentation:
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component to the root App component as recommended
- No additional configuration in vercel.json was required

### Testing & Verification

✅ **Build Test:** Successfully ran `npm run build` - the project builds without errors
✅ **Bundle Size:** Build completed in 697ms with all assets properly optimized
✅ **No Linter:** The project doesn't have ESLint configured, so no linting errors to check
✅ **No Tests:** The project doesn't have a test suite configured

### Implementation Notes

- The Analytics component was placed at the root level of the application to ensure tracking across all pages and views
- The implementation is non-intrusive and preserves all existing functionality
- The component will automatically collect web vitals and page views once deployed to Vercel
- Analytics will need to be enabled in the Vercel dashboard under the project's Analytics settings

### Next Steps for Activation

To activate Web Analytics for this project:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the project's settings in the Vercel dashboard
3. Enable Web Analytics under the Analytics section
4. Analytics data will start appearing after the next deployment and user visits
